This product bundles one engine sidecar, maleficium-engine, built by
scripts/build-engine.sh and packed into the installable next to the app
binary. It contains:

- Tectonic 0.17.0, built from its published source, MIT-licensed.
- latexml 0.7.6 (latexml-oxide), built from its published source, released
  under CC0 1.0; its dependencies carry their own licences (see the
  engine's Cargo.lock).
- The SyncTeX parser from jlaurens/synctex at commit
  04cf8e3e8665ff203248d7af78ee1129afbc1b64, vendored unmodified in
  src-tauri/engine/synctex under its MIT licence (Copyright Jerome Laurens
  2008-2024).

This product bundles, inlined into the built-in widget runtimes under
src-tauri/widget-runtimes/ (built by `npm run build:runtimes`, no network at
build or run time), the Vega visualization stack and its dependencies, all
permissively licensed (checked against package-lock.json, 2026-10-01):

- vega 6.4.0, vega-lite 6.4.3 and vega-interpreter 2.3.2, Copyright (c)
  2015-present the Vega project and UW Interactive Data Lab, BSD-3-Clause.
- Their 76 transitive dependencies (d3-* and topojson-client under ISC or
  BSD-3-Clause; fast-deep-equal, json-stringify-pretty-compact and similar
  under MIT; tslib under 0BSD; robust-predicates under Unlicense).

The model runtime under src-tauri/widget-runtimes/model/ also inlines three.js
0.186.1 (its GLTFLoader and OrbitControls included), Copyright (c) 2010-2026
three.js authors, MIT, with no dependencies (checked against package-lock.json,
2026-10-01). Its type declarations, @types/three 0.186.0 (MIT) and their
dependencies (MIT, Apache-2.0), are build-time only and not bundled. The video
runtime uses only the browser's own <video> element.

The model and video test fixtures under e2e/fixtures/ (a generated glb cube and
an ffmpeg test pattern, e2e/fixtures/gen-media.py) are original to Maleficium
and dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0.

